# GPT Fast Path (Non-MSC Only)

Applies to GPT-5.6 Sol and other GPT coding models.

## Hard exclusion: MSC

This rule is inactive for MSC research, MSC `X.c` edits, unit script ports, and
MSC-coupled motion/model/Param/HUD work. Do not activate caveman,
`gpt-fast-path`, or `gpt-fast-verify` for those tasks. Route through
`.cursor/skills/msc-research-index/SKILL.md` and perform the complete lifecycle,
state-ownership, reverse-transition, and resource-existence audit. MSC may use
multiple evidence paths and multiple staged verification gates.

- Communicate in caveman style: outcome, blocker, next action only.
- Use one evidence path. CodeGraph answers structure; `rg` answers literals.
  Do not cross-confirm deterministic success.
- Batch reads. Avoid broad scans, repeated reads, speculative audits, and
  unrelated cleanup.
- Completion requires fresh evidence from exactly one smallest semantic
  verifier. Exact behavioral test > nearest module test > narrow build/type/
  syntax/schema check.
- Pass means stop. Failure permits diagnosis plus one rerun of the same gate.
- Never stack build, typecheck, lint, tests, coverage, audit, E2E, and full
  suites by default. Docs/rules/skills do not trigger app tests.
- Expand only for explicit user request, release work, or material security/
  data-loss risk. Ask before a full suite when practical.

This rule narrows generic verification skills. It does not remove the need for
fresh evidence.

